    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-51145",
      "knowledge_point_id": "5c6490a5-4923-58e8-99c3-d568a033800e",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing Coefficients in a Partial Fractions Decomposition",
      "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}-3x+5}{({x}^{2}+2)(x-1)}=\\frac{2x+B}{{x}^{2}+2}+\\frac{2}{x-1},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $({x}^{2}+2)(x-1)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-3x+5 & =(2x+B)(x-1)+2({x}^{2}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}-3(0)+5 & =(2(0)+B)(0-1)+2({0}^{2}+2) \\\\ 5 & =(B)(-1)+2(2) \\\\ 5 & =-B+4 \\\\ 1 & =-B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
